---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
const faqs = [
  { q: 'How do I make a seating plan for a classroom?', a: 'Enter the number of rows and columns, add student names or a roll number range, choose an order and press Make seating plan. Print it or copy it to a spreadsheet.' },
  { q: 'Can I leave gaps between students for an exam?', a: 'Yes. Choose "Every other seat in a row", "Every other row" or "Checkerboard" under spacing. Blocked seats are marked with a cross and are never filled.' },
  { q: 'What does the snake order do?', a: 'Row one runs left to right, row two right to left, and so on. It keeps consecutive roll numbers close together at the row ends.' },
  { q: 'Is the student list stored anywhere?', a: 'No. Names are used only in your browser while the page is open. Closing or refreshing the page clears them, and nothing is sent to a server.' },
  { q: 'What if there are more students than seats?', a: 'The tool seats as many as it can and lists the rest in red, so you know to add a row or column.' },
];
---
<ToolLayout slug="seating-plan-generator" faqs={faqs}>
  {/* AUTHOR REVIEW: lead paragraph, drafted by AI. */}
  <p slot="lead">
    This seating plan generator builds a printable classroom or exam hall chart in seconds. Enter rows, columns and your
    student names or roll numbers, pick an order, and print the plan or copy it to a spreadsheet.
  </p>

  <div slot="tool">
    <div class="no-print">
      <div class="field"><label for="sp-title">Title (optional)</label><input id="sp-title" type="text" placeholder="e.g. Class 9B, Science test, Room 12" maxlength="80" /></div>
      <div class="row two">
        <div class="field"><label for="sp-rows">Rows</label><input id="sp-rows" type="number" min="1" max="30" value="5" inputmode="numeric" /></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="sp-cols">Columns (seats per row)</label><input id="sp-cols" type="number" min="1" max="30" value="6" inputmode="numeric" /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="sp-source">Students</label>
        <select id="sp-source"><option value="names">Type or paste names</option><option value="range">Roll number range</option></select>
      </div>
      <div class="field" id="sp-namebox">
        <label for="sp-names">One name per line</label>
        <textarea id="sp-names" placeholder="Asha Verma&#10;Rahul Singh&#10;Meena Iyer"></textarea>
      </div>
      <div class="row three" id="sp-rangebox" hidden>
        <div class="field"><label for="sp-from">From roll number</label><input id="sp-from" type="number" value="1" inputmode="numeric" /></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="sp-to">To roll number</label><input id="sp-to" type="number" value="30" inputmode="numeric" /></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="sp-prefix">Prefix (optional)</label><input id="sp-prefix" type="text" placeholder="e.g. 9B-" maxlength="10" /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="row two">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="sp-order">Seating order</label>
          <select id="sp-order"><option value="row">In order, row by row</option><option value="snake">Snake (alternate direction)</option><option value="random">Random shuffle</option></select>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="sp-gap">Spacing</label>
          <select id="sp-gap"><option value="none">Use every seat</option><option value="alt-col">Every other seat in a row</option><option value="alt-row">Every other row</option><option value="check">Checkerboard</option></select>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" id="sp-go" class="btn">Make seating plan</button></div>
      <p id="sp-status" class="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Fill in the details and press the button.</p>
    </div>
    <div id="sp-result" hidden>
      <h2 id="sp-heading" style="margin-top:.5em">Seating plan</h2>
      <div id="sp-plan"></div>
      <div class="btn-row no-print">
        <button type="button" id="sp-print" class="btn">Print</button>
        <button type="button" id="sp-shuffle" class="btn secondary" hidden>Shuffle again</button>
        <button type="button" id="sp-copy" class="btn secondary">Copy as text</button>
        <button type="button" id="sp-csv" class="btn secondary">Download CSV</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* AUTHOR REVIEW: how-to and worked example drafted by AI. Add your own exam-hall experience. */}
  <h2>How to make a seating plan</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Type the number of rows and the number of seats in each row.</li>
    <li>Paste your class list, one name per line, or switch to a roll number range.</li>
    <li>Choose the order. Random shuffle is useful for tests; row by row suits a normal class.</li>
    <li>Pick a spacing option if you need empty seats between students, then press Make seating plan.</li>
    <li>Print the chart, copy it, or download it as a CSV file.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Worked example</h2>
  <p class="worked">
    You have 28 students and a room with 5 rows of 6 seats, which is 30 seats. Paste the names, choose Random shuffle
    and press the button. All 28 students are placed, two seats stay empty and the chart is ready to print. If you
    choose Checkerboard instead, only 15 seats are usable, so the tool seats 15 students and lists the other 13 in red.
  </p>
  <h2>Tips for a fair plan</h2>
  <p>
    Count your seats before you start: with spacing turned on, a room holds fewer students than its desks suggest.
    Stand at the back of the room when you read the plan, because "Front of the room" is at the top of the chart.
    Keep the printed copy with your attendance record.
  </p>
  <script>import '../../scripts/seating.js';</script>
</ToolLayout>
